1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,406
A trading bot is easy to advertise.

2
00:00:02,406 --> 00:00:04,254
But what did you actually buy?

3
00:00:04,254 --> 00:00:05,178
Meet Prooflot.

4
00:00:06,253 --> 00:00:08,477
Creators upload their own Python bot.

5
00:00:08,477 --> 00:00:10,882
The source stays private until purchase.

6
00:00:11,532 --> 00:00:13,183
Choose the data and costs.

7
00:00:13,183 --> 00:00:16,930
This walkthrough uses synthetic data and simulated payment.

8
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:21,633
The bot runs in an isolated container, with no network access.

9
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:23,660
Fees and slippage are included.

10
00:00:24,603 --> 00:00:28,827
Review returns, drawdown, and a buy and hold baseline before deciding.

11
00:00:29,714 --> 00:00:31,549
Three trades are a small sample.

12
00:00:31,549 --> 00:00:33,212
The limitations stay visible.

13
00:00:33,862 --> 00:00:37,041
Set the price and publish the exact version you inspected.

14
00:00:37,691 --> 00:00:39,375
Buyers see the report first.

15
00:00:39,375 --> 00:00:42,683
The version hash binds the listing to one specific bot.

16
00:00:43,333 --> 00:00:46,469
Check the version, price, and license terms at checkout.

17
00:00:47,404 --> 00:00:49,921
The purchased version is now in your library.

18
00:00:50,571 --> 00:00:55,798
Download the actual source, report, license, and offline verifier in one zip file.

19
00:00:56,448 --> 00:00:59,349
Then run the purchased code again in a fresh container.

20
00:01:03,587 --> 00:01:05,985
All seventy three decisions completed.

21
00:01:05,985 --> 00:01:08,067
The deterministic result matches.

22
00:01:08,717 --> 00:01:11,021
Here is a real NEAR testnet listing.

23
00:01:11,021 --> 00:01:11,917
It lost money.

24
00:01:11,917 --> 00:01:13,709
That result remains visible.

25
00:01:14,359 --> 00:01:19,010
Verify the version, report, terms, and price against final contract state.

26
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:23,734
Compare performance across four fixed Bitcoin and Ethereum cases.

27
00:01:24,384 --> 00:01:29,184
Every started attempt is retained, including losses and higher cost sensitivity.

28
00:01:29,834 --> 00:01:32,838
NEAR records the commitment and result hashes.

29
00:01:32,838 --> 00:01:35,189
Execution remains operator attested.

30
00:01:35,839 --> 00:01:39,443
Try the deployed service at Prooflot dot Vercel dot app.

31
00:01:39,443 --> 00:01:41,087
No local server is needed.

32
00:01:42,849 --> 00:01:46,476
The code, testnet receipts, and verification tools are public.

33
00:01:47,126 --> 00:01:47,766
Prooflot.

34
00:01:47,766 --> 00:01:50,262
Inspect, buy, download, and test again.
